<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47895" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαρσᾰλ-έος</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαρρᾰλέος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάρσος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>daring</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολεμιστής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.589
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦτορ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					19.169
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωνά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					9.49
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλπίδες θ</span>.
			<i>confident</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				536
			</span></i> (lyr.): c. inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ
				τῶν ἵππων πολεμεῖν θαρρ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				350a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. περί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1383a15
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>PA</u>
					667a16
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
			</span></i>l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ θαρσαλέον</span>
			<i>confidence</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τῷ θαρσαλέῳ εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.51
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				21.25
			</span></i>: so in Adv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαρραλέως
				ἔχειν</span> to be <i>of good courage</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς θάνατον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					34e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τοὺς πολεμίους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					2.6.14
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					7.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in bad sense,
				<i>overbold, audacious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. καὶ ἀναιδής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.449
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαρσαλέη, κύον ἀδεές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					19.91
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. καὶ θρασεῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					649c
				</span></i>
			. Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψευδῆ λέγειν θαρραλέως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Is.
					10.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>that which may be ventured on</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ
			θ</span>., opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δεινά</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				359c
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				<u>La.</u>
				195c
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἀληθῆ . . λέγειν ἀσφαλὲς
				καὶ θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>R.</u>
				450e
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
